      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T18:15:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why even specify a boundary? Doesn\u0027t that just needlessly limit you?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1617,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 1617,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "dd9ac6f91629a2de28370e4a30209718681180db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17c1c8e7_8a3a98c7",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1617,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T23:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using a value \u003c 2 can be actively harmful - 0 can just disarm the timer, which may cause some indefinite behavior. For the upper limit I can use a larger value if you like (say 20) but there is definitely a point after which it is non-sensical.",
      "parentUuid": "88939e7d_047cba09",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1617,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 1617,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "dd9ac6f91629a2de28370e4a30209718681180db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
