      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T18:15:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know if this setting is used and who sets it and on what devices? If it isn\u0027t used, can it be deprecated / removed and use the phenotype-configurable value instead? (it was added a long time ago: ag/216256).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13256,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 13257,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "dd9ac6f91629a2de28370e4a30209718681180db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df4fdaff_1aa22a8b",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 13257,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T23:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not used in aosp code, but OEMs may be using this. I want to be safe and continue honoring the value that they set. E.g. an OEM in Brazil may have a clear deal with their carrier to pull the best timeout is from their special carrier app.\n\nIf you\u0027re sure about this -  I am fine with removing it. Just didn\u0027t think it was necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "ecbc4cf5_6af4a5b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13256,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 13257,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "dd9ac6f91629a2de28370e4a30209718681180db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
